{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-27-1","title":"Jeremiah 27:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Under the type of bonds and yokes he prophesies the subduing of the neighbour kings unto Nebuchadnezzar. 8 He exhorts them to yield, and not to believe the false prophets. 12 The like he does to Zedekiah. 19 He foretells the remnant of the vessels shall be carried to Babylon, and there continue until the day of visitation.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3409. B.C. 595. the beginning. 3,12,19,20; 26:1; 28:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-2","title":"Jeremiah 27:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>saith the Lord. or, hath the Lord said. Am 7:1,4 Make. 12; 28:10-14 put. 13:1-11; 18:2-10; 19:1-11; 28:10; 1Ki 11:30,31; Isa 20:2-4 Eze 4:1-5:17; 12:1-28; 24:3-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-3","title":"Jeremiah 27:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Edom. 25:19-26; 47:1-49:39; Eze 25:1-28:26; 29:18; Am 1:9-15; 2:1-3 the messengers. 2Ch 36:13; Eze 17:15-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-4","title":"Jeremiah 27:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>to say unto their masters, Thus. or, concerning theirmasters, saying, Thus. the Lord. 10:10,16; 25:27; 51:19; Ex 5:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-5","title":"Jeremiah 27:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>made. 10:11,12; 32:17; 51:15; Ge 9:6; Ex 20:11; Job 26:5-14; 38:4-41 Ps 102:25; 136:5-9; 146:5,6; 148:2-5; Isa 40:21-26; 42:5; 44:24 Isa 45:12; 48:13; 51:13; Joh 1:1-3; Ac 14:15; 17:24; Col 1:16 Heb 1:2,10,11; Re 4:11 and have. Ge 1:29,30; 9:2,3; De 2:7,9,19; 5:16; 32:8; Jos 1:2,3; Ezr 1:2 Ps 115:15,16; 135:10-12; De 2:21; 4:17,25,32,35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-6","title":"Jeremiah 27:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>I given all. 28:14; Da 2:37,38; 5:18,19 my. 24:1; 25:9; 43:10; 51:20-23; Isa 44:28; Eze 29:18-20 and. 28:14; Ps 50:10-12; Da 2:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-7","title":"Jeremiah 27:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>all. 25:11-14; 50:9,10; 52:31; 2Ch 36:20,21 until. 25:12; 50:27; Ps 37:13; 137:8,9; Isa 13:1,8-22; 14:22,23; 21:9 Isa 47:1-5 Da 5:25-31; Hab 2:7; Zec 2:8,9; Re 13:5-10; 14:8,15-20; 16:19 Re 17:16,17; 18:2-8 many. 25:14; 50:1-51:64; Isa 14:4-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-8","title":"Jeremiah 27:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>And it.There is a peculiar grandeur, as well as propriety, in this method of predicting Nebuchadnezzar's rapid successes. The God of Israel, declaring himself to be the Lord of armies, and the Creator and Owner of the whole earth, with all its inhabitants and productions, and claiming full sovereignty over his creatures, avows his determination, for reasons he does not deign to assign, to give all the countries of the world to the king of Babylon, whom he calls his servant, because he would accomplish an important part of his most righteous designs. They, therefore, who would escape the most dreadful judgments, must submit to the God of Israel, by submitting to Nebuchadnezzar; they must hearken to the prophets of Israel, and not to their own diviners; and they must observe, that Nebuchadnezzar, his son, and his grandson, would whatever opposition should be made, possess the full dominion of all these countries, till the appointed time was expired; and then, these haughty conquerors would in their turn become the prey of other powerful conquerors; all of which was most exactly fulfilled.</p>\n<p>that nation. 25:28,29; 38:17-19; 40:9; 42:10-18; 52:3-6; Eze 17:19-21 with the sword. 24:10; Eze 14:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-9","title":"Jeremiah 27:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>hearken. 14-16; 14:14; 23:16,25,32; 29:8; Ex 7:11; De 18:10-12,14 Jos 13:22; *marg: Isa 8:19; Mic 3:7; Zec 10:2; Mal 3:5; Ac 8:11; Re 9:21; 18:23; 21:8 Re 22:15 dreamers. Heb. dreams. Isa 47:12-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-10","title":"Jeremiah 27:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>they. 14; 28:16; Eze 14:9-11 to. 32:31; La 2:14 I. 15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-11","title":"Jeremiah 27:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>to bring. 2,8,12 those. 21:9; 38:2; 40:9-12; 42:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-12","title":"Jeremiah 27:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Zedekiah. 3; 28:1; 38:17; 2Ch 36:11-13; Pr 1:33; Eze 17:11-21 Bring. 2,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-13","title":"Jeremiah 27:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Why. 38:20; Pr 8:36; Eze 18:24,31; 33:11 by the sword. 8; 24:9; 38:2; Eze 14:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-14","title":"Jeremiah 27:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>hearken. 9; Isa 28:10-13; 2Co 11:13-15; Php 3:2 they. 10; 14:14; 23:21,25; 28:15; 29:8,9; 1Ki 22:22,23; Eze 13:6-15,22,23 Mic 2:11; Mt 7:15; 2Pe 2:1-3; 1Jo 4:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-15","title":"Jeremiah 27:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>a lie. Heb. in a lie, or lyingly. that I. 10; 2Ch 18:17-22; 25:16; Eze 14:3-10; Mt 24:24; 2Th 2:9-12 2Ti 2:17-19; 4:3,4; Re 13:7,8,12-14 ye. 6:13-15; 8:10-12; 14:15,16; 20:6; 23:15; 28:16,17; 29:22,23,31,32 Mic 3:5-7; Mt 15:14; Re 19:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-16","title":"Jeremiah 27:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Behold. 28:3; 2Ki 24:13; 2Ch 36:7-10; Da 1:2 for. 10,14; Isa 9:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-17","title":"Jeremiah 27:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>serve. 11,12 wherefore. 13; 38:17,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-18","title":"Jeremiah 27:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>they. 1Ki 18:24,26 let them. 7:16; 15:1; 18:20; 42:2; Ge 18:24-33; 20:17; 1Sa 7:8; 12:19,23 2Ch 32:20; Job 42:8,9; Eze 14:14,18-20; 22:30; Mal 1:9; Jas 5:16-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-19","title":"Jeremiah 27:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>the pillars. 52:17-23; 1Ki 7:15-22; 2Ki 25:13,17; 2Ch 4:2-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-20","title":"Jeremiah 27:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>when. 22:28 Coniah. 24:1; 2Ki 24:14-16 Jehoiachin. 2Ch 36:10,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-27-22","title":"Jeremiah 27:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>carried. 29:10; 34:5; 52:17-21; 2Ki 24:13-17; 2Ch 36:17,18; Da 5:1-4,23 until. 25:11,12; 29:10; 32:5; 2Ch 36:21-23; Ezr 1:1-5; Pr 21:30; Da 9:2 then. Ezr 1:7,11; 5:13-15; 7:9,19</p>"}]}